resolutions.rationale:
The finding is correct. D1 says "baseUrl on api.anthropic.com" with no matching rule. A `startsWith` or `includes` test admits a proxy, which breaks the spec's promise that a proxy keeps a byte-identical payload.

**Measured:**
- `https://api.anthropic.com.corp-proxy.internal` passes `startsWith`;
- `https://gw.corp/api.anthropic.com/` and `http://localhost:8080/https://api.anthropic.com` pass `includes`;
- `new URL(baseUrl).hostname === "api.anthropic.com"` rejects all three, accepts pi's own `https://api.anthropic.com` (with a trailing slash, a `:443` port or mixed case too), and rejects a bare host, garbage, an empty string and undefined, provided the `new URL` throw is caught.

resolutions.required_change:
**D1.** "baseUrl on api.anthropic.com" becomes:

> "a baseUrl whose `new URL(baseUrl).hostname` is `api.anthropic.com`; a missing baseUrl, or one `new URL` cannot parse, is uncovered"

**Spec requirement "Only routes the predicate covers change".** "a baseUrl on api.anthropic.com" becomes "a baseUrl whose host is exactly api.anthropic.com".

**Spec proxy scenario.** In the WHEN, name both proxy shapes, a host that merely starts with or contains `api.anthropic.com`, so that each goes out byte-identical.

**§8.1 route table.** Add four rows:
- `https://api.anthropic.com.corp-proxy.internal` → `undefined`;
- `https://gw.corp/api.anthropic.com/` → `undefined`;
- a missing baseUrl → `undefined`;
- `https://api.anthropic.com` → edited.

